christina vogg cares for her sick father  as well as her three children when she's  not busy at home  she works as a film producer and she  expects fair pay  but as is the case for so many women men  in her field earn more for the same work  germany has a gender wage gap of 22  percent one of the largest in the eu  demonstrators in berlin say that has to  stop  we are all equal under the law so it  doesn't make sense  when we have children it's a question of  who stays home who does the housework  and looks after the kids  and it comes down to who you see  i don't know if men earn all that much  more than women inequality in the  workplace is being addressed  we're on the right  but women's path minister manuela  schwesik is far from satisfied  she plans to introduce an equal wages  law that would require companies to  reveal inequalities  every company every administration  should ask itself  how high is the wage gap what are the  reasons for it and what can we do about  it says change also needs to happen at  home  only when men and women equally share  housework and child care  where women have more time to climb the  ladder at work
 

